
---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/layout/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Customer Support Automation | Maditron"
  description="An end-to-end customer support automation project combining AI assistance and human support in one seamless customer experience."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main>
    <section class="section project-detail-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <a href="/projects/" class="project-back-link">← All Projects</a>

        <div class="kicker">PROJECT / 01 · AI & AUTOMATION</div>

        <h1>Customer Support Operations Automation</h1>

        <p class="project-detail-intro">
          A customer support system where AI and human agents work together
          to handle customer requests — while maintaining one consistent
          experience for the customer.
        </p>

        <div class="resume-skills">
          <span>AI Automation</span>
          <span>Human-in-the-Loop</span>
          <span>Workflow Automation</span>
          <span>Customer Support</span>
        <a
  class="github-link"
  href="https://github.com/Maditron/local-first-ai-customer-support-automation"
  target="_blank"
  rel="noopener noreferrer"
>
  GitHub ↗
</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      
    </section>

    

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container project-detail-content">

        <!-- ABOUT -->

        <div class="project-case-section">
          <div class="kicker">01 / ABOUT</div>
          <h2>About the Project</h2>

          <p>
            Customer support often involves handling the same types of
            questions repeatedly. Some requests are straightforward and can
            be handled automatically, while others require human judgment,
            experience, and attention.
          </p>

          <p>
            I built this project around a simple idea: AI should take care
            of what can be automated, while human agents remain available
            whenever their involvement is needed.
          </p>

          <p>
            The important part is that both operate as part of the same
            support process. Whether a response comes from an AI system
            or a human agent, the customer receives it through the same
            support experience, without having to distinguish between them.
          </p>

          <p>
            The goal is not simply to replace support agents with AI.
            It's to combine automation and human involvement into one
            coherent way of handling customer requests.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- TECHNICAL CHALLENGES -->

        <div class="project-case-section">
          <div class="kicker">02 / ENGINEERING</div>
          <h2>Technical Challenges</h2>

          <h3>Knowing when to automate</h3>
          <p>
            Not every customer request should be handled automatically.
            The system needs to distinguish between requests suitable
            for automated handling and cases that need human attention.
          </p>

          <h3>Maintaining response consistency</h3>
          <p>
            AI-generated and human-written responses need to belong to
            the same conversation flow. The customer should not have
            to deal with separate channels or different support experiences.
          </p>

          <h3>Keeping humans in control</h3>
          <p>
            Automation should not mean giving an AI unrestricted authority.
            Human involvement needs to remain possible when a request
            is unclear, sensitive, or requires additional judgment.
          </p>

          <h3>Handling the complete conversation</h3>
          <p>
            Customer support is more than generating a single response.
            Requests need to be processed in context, routed appropriately,
            and followed through until they are resolved.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- WHAT IT SOLVES -->

        <div class="project-case-section">
          <div class="kicker">03 / END-TO-END PROCESS</div>
          <h2>What It Solves</h2>

          <p>
            The system brings the customer support process into one
            automated workflow, from the first incoming message to
            the final response.
          </p>

          <div class="support-workflow">

            <div class="support-workflow-step">
              <span class="workflow-number">01</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Request received</h3>
                <p>
                  A customer submits a support request through the
                  connected support channel.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="support-workflow-step">
              <span class="workflow-number">02</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Request processed</h3>
                <p>
                  The request is analyzed and its content and context
                  are used to determine how it should be handled.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="support-workflow-step">
              <span class="workflow-number">03</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Handling decision</h3>
                <p>
                  The workflow determines whether the request can
                  proceed through automated handling or needs
                  human involvement.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="support-workflow-step">
              <span class="workflow-number">04</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Response prepared</h3>
                <p>
                  AI prepares a response for automated handling,
                  or a human agent reviews and writes the response
                  when human involvement is required.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="support-workflow-step">
              <span class="workflow-number">05</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Response delivered</h3>
                <p>
                  The response is delivered through the same customer
                  support experience, regardless of who prepared it.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="support-highlight">
            <h3>One support experience. Two ways of handling requests.</h3>
            <p>
              AI and human agents work behind the scenes.
              From the customer's perspective, it's one continuous
              support conversation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- PICTURES -->

        <div class="project-case-section">
          <div class="kicker">04 / GALLERY</div>
          <h2>Pictures</h2>

          <p>
            A closer look at the actual workflows and implementation.
          </p>

          <div class="project-gallery">
        <img
            src="/images/projects/customersupport.png"
            alt="Customer Support Automation project"
            loading="lazy"
        />
        </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
